{
"title": "IWST 2026: International Workshop on Smalltalk Technologies"
}

!About IWST 26 

IWST 26 — International Workshop on Smalltalk Technologies
Plovdiv Bulgaria; July 7th to 10th, 2026
Co-located with ESUG 2026
*IWST 2026 Call for Submissions>https://conf.researchr.org/track/iwst-2026/iwst-2026-papers#Call-for-Submissions*

!! Description

The goals of the workshop is to create a forum around contributions and experiences in building or using technologies related to Smalltalk. While maturity of presented ideas and results is not crucial, it is expected that their presentation triggers discussion and exchange of ideas. The topics of your paper can be on all aspect of Smalltalk, theoretical as well as practical.
Authors are invited to submit research articles or industrial papers. 

From this year we will be using the *conf.researchr.org>https://conf.researchr.org/* platform to maintain *IWST website>https://conf.researchr.org/home/iwst-2026/*, while this page will provide important ESUG-related information such as one about the organization, registration, etc.

!! Registration

- Early *registration>https://registration.esug.org/* deadline: April 1, 2026

""IMPORTANT"": As the *submissions deadline>https://conf.researchr.org/track/iwst-2026/iwst-2026-papers#Call-for-Submissions* for IWST is after the early registration deadline, we have got the confirmation that our authors are allowed to fill in the registration form by the deadline for early registration if they plan to submit the presentation abstract, and to pay afterwards in case of the acceptance. Therefore, "please fill in the registration form before the 1st of April." 


